  "biography": {
    "plain_text": "Cornelius Vanderbilt Crane was an American heir, naturalist and philanthropist who used his family’s industrial fortune to support scientific exploration. He led and financed the Field Museum’s Pacific expedition, whose global voyage collected thousands of specimens. Crane later supported medical research in French Polynesia and helped preserve a Tahitian botanical garden.",
